{"study_id": "zk26_lgbm_defaults_20261106_haiku_mcts", "search_seed": 42, "factor_id": "90e4688062e59f50abe6d8c6a4184373099ec0a7ef106b2530577fd48ad99efb", "expression": "DELAY(IF_THEN_ELSE(GT($zk_rbasis12, TS_MEDIAN($zk_rbasis12, 1440.0)), TS_ZSCORE($adj_close@15m, 32.0), 0.0), 2.0)", "canonical_expression": {"op": "DELAY", "args": [{"op": "IF_THEN_ELSE", "args": [{"op": "GT", "args": [{"op": "field", "args": [], "value": "zk_rbasis12"}, {"op": "TS_MEDIAN", "args": [{"op": "field", "args": [], "value": "zk_rbasis12"}, {"op": "const", "args": [], "value": 1440.0}], "value": null}], "value": null}, {"op": "TS_ZSCORE", "args": [{"op": "field", "args": [], "value": "adj_close@15m"}, {"op": "const", "args": [], "value": 32.0}], "value": null}, {"op": "const", "args": [], "value": 0.0}], "value": null}, {"op": "const", "args": [], "value": 2.0}], "value": null}, "description": "Trial 20 used a 120-bar 60m stretch, about five trading days, while the target is a 12-bar 5m log return, about one hour. This candidate moves the stretch to a 32-bar 15m z-score, about eight hours, so its horizon is closer to the label. The z-score normalizes magnitude across products for pooled IC. The extreme-basis gate passes the stretch only when zk_rbasis12 is above its own 1440-bar rolling median, and outputs zero otherwise. The 2-bar delay is kept from the parent. The expression uses only allowed fields and operators with concrete integer windows and no validation errors. Overlap with admitted zk_basis12, zk_rbasis, zk_dmaOI and zk_dOI members is untested and must pass the |corr| < 0.7 deduplication check. No performance is claimed.", "direction": 1, "origins": [{"source": "mcts_llm", "trial": 21, "attempt": 21, "run_id": "futures_kernel_5m_full-all-fold2-mcts_llm-42-64f65a23b9"}]}
{"study_id": "zk26_lgbm_defaults_20261106_haiku_mcts", "search_seed": 42, "factor_id": "e568c7b5f9c504a1164bbe5efeaca8380c8b626db84bf4f4cd2b12adce77e78c", "expression": "IF_THEN_ELSE(GT(TS_RANK(TS_MEAN($amount, 288.0), 288.0), 0.5), NEG(TS_MEAN(FILLNA(DIVIDE(SUBTRACT(SUBTRACT($adj_close, $adj_low), SUBTRACT($adj_high, $adj_close)), SUBTRACT($adj_high, $adj_low)), 0.0), 12.0)), 0.0)", "canonical_expression": {"op": "IF_THEN_ELSE", "args": [{"op": "GT", "args": [{"op": "TS_RANK", "args": [{"op": "TS_MEAN", "args": [{"op": "field", "args": [], "value": "amount"}, {"op": "const", "args": [], "value": 288.0}], "value": null}, {"op": "const", "args": [], "value": 288.0}], "value": null}, {"op": "const", "args": [], "value": 0.5}], "value": null}, {"op": "NEG", "args": [{"op": "TS_MEAN", "args": [{"op": "FILLNA", "args": [{"op": "DIVIDE", "args": [{"op": "SUBTRACT", "args": [{"op": "SUBTRACT", "args": [{"op": "field", "args": [], "value": "adj_close"}, {"op": "field", "args": [], "value": "adj_low"}], "value": null}, {"op": "SUBTRACT", "args": [{"op": "field", "args": [], "value": "adj_high"}, {"op": "field", "args": [], "value": "adj_close"}], "value": null}], "value": null}, {"op": "SUBTRACT", "args": [{"op": "field", "args": [], "value": "adj_high"}, {"op": "field", "args": [], "value": "adj_low"}], "value": null}], "value": null}, {"op": "const", "args": [], "value": 0.0}], "value": null}, {"op": "const", "args": [], "value": 12.0}], "value": null}], "value": null}, {"op": "const", "args": [], "value": 0.0}], "value": null}, "description": "Closing-pressure exhaustion should revert over the 12-bar (about one-hour) horizon. CLV places each 5m close within its high-low range, and its 12-bar mean measures sustained buying or selling pressure, with NEG setting the reversal sign explicitly. The weighted IC is metric-diluted: the pooled score weights products by sqrt(sum(amount)), and the equal-weighted train Spearman is about twice the weighted value, so the signal may be concentrated in thin products. The prior CS_ZSCORE and volume-shock variant (2d82a007) lowered weighted train IC to 0.0008, so this candidate drops the volume multiplier and cross-sectional scaling. Instead it gates on each product's own liquidity: a 288-bar mean of amount is ranked against its own 288-bar history with TS_RANK, and the signal is active only when that rank is above the median. The 288-bar mean smooths unadjusted amount jumps at contract rolls, and the within-product rank needs no cross-product scaling. The expression uses only allowed fields and operators with concrete positive integer windows. It is syntactically valid, with well under 100 nodes. Overlap with fa6ea148 and 26279e70 must pass the |corr| < 0.7 check, and the lag-1 RankIC gap should be watched because the parent showed fast decay. No performance is claimed.", "direction": 1, "origins": [{"source": "mcts_llm", "trial": 84, "attempt": 84, "run_id": "futures_kernel_5m_full-all-fold2-mcts_llm-42-64f65a23b9"}]}
{"study_id": "zk26_lgbm_defaults_20261106_haiku_mcts", "search_seed": 42, "factor_id": "1d580ef7f09fe23d8ab3144c567a16d178b1ce457a37f79d48a73f272ed876f1", "expression": "FILLNA(CS_ZSCORE(MULTIPLY(TS_ZSCORE($adj_close@15m, 32.0), DIVIDE(1.0, ADD(1.0, EXP(NEG(CLIP(TS_ZSCORE(FILLNA($zk_rbasis12, 0.0), 1440.0), -3.0, 3.0))))))), 0.0)", "canonical_expression": {"op": "FILLNA", "args": [{"op": "CS_ZSCORE", "args": [{"op": "MULTIPLY", "args": [{"op": "TS_ZSCORE", "args": [{"op": "field", "args": [], "value": "adj_close@15m"}, {"op": "const", "args": [], "value": 32.0}], "value": null}, {"op": "DIVIDE", "args": [{"op": "const", "args": [], "value": 1.0}, {"op": "ADD", "args": [{"op": "const", "args": [], "value": 1.0}, {"op": "EXP", "args": [{"op": "NEG", "args": [{"op": "CLIP", "args": [{"op": "TS_ZSCORE", "args": [{"op": "FILLNA", "args": [{"op": "field", "args": [], "value": "zk_rbasis12"}, {"op": "const", "args": [], "value": 0.0}], "value": null}, {"op": "const", "args": [], "value": 1440.0}], "value": null}, {"op": "const", "args": [], "value": -3.0}, {"op": "const", "args": [], "value": 3.0}], "value": null}], "value": null}], "value": null}], "value": null}], "value": null}], "value": null}], "value": null}, {"op": "const", "args": [], "value": 0.0}], "value": null}, "description": "A 32-bar 15m adjusted-close stretch (about eight hours) is hypothesized to continue over the next hour (12 five-minute bars), with the continuation stronger when the product's basis term-structure state, $zk_rbasis12, is unusually high against its own 1440-bar history (about five trading days). The previous candidate used a hard IF_THEN_ELSE switch against a rolling median, which was rejected for low coverage (0.62 against 0.8), likely because null monthly-field warmup rows propagated as unknown through the switch. This version replaces the switch with a continuous logistic soft weight. The basis state is null-filled to 0.0 and its rolling z-score is clipped to [-3, 3] before the logisti